===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*men- (stand out)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|manace}}, from {{der|en|fro|manace}}, {{m|fro|menace}}, &c., from {{der|en|LL.|minācia||[[threat]], menace}}, from {{der|en|la|mināx||[[threatening]]}} + {{m|la|-ia||''[[form]]ing [[abstract]] [[noun]]s''}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[perceived]] [[threat]] or [[danger]]. {{defdate|a. 1300}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis|9|passage=the dark '''menace''' of the distant war.}}
# The act of [[threatening]].
# {{lb|en|informal}} An [[annoying]] and [[bothersome]] person or thing.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|the act or process of threatening, a tendancy to threaten}} {{l|en|minacity}}, {{l|en|minacy}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|yellow menace}

